    "description": {
      "chat": "",
      "unidentified": "",
      "value": "<p>Normal vegetation in the 30-foot-radius area becomes diseased and stops producing seeds or fruit. Any living creature that touches blighted ground at any time during its turn must make a Fortitude save or contract blight plague; spell resistance applies to this infection. Turning checks made on the ground take a -2 profane penalty, while rebuke-undead checks gain a +2 profane bonus; spell resistance does not affect either modifier.</p><p>Blight plague is a supernatural disease with a 1-minute incubation period that deals 1d4 temporary Intellect damage. It does not end naturally: it continues until the victim reaches Intellect 0 or receives <em>remove disease</em> or similar magic. A humanoid reduced to Intellect 0 by it immediately becomes a zombie.</p><p>The printed component line includes a material component, but the spell gives no material description or cost.</p><p><strong>Automation boundary:</strong> Mark the permanent terrain, test each turn's contact, track supernatural disease and Intellect damage, transform humanoids at 0, and adjust turning or rebuking checks manually.</p>"
    },
